SUMMARY:Monday Blues: Angelica Jones
DESCRIPTION:Ease into your week with Monday Blues at Union Summer\, featuring two shows of blues music showcasing a range of artists. \nAngelica Jones is a Canadian blues-rock artist known for her raw\, soulful\, and commanding sound. Her music blends gritty blues with rock-driven energy and emotional storytelling\, delivered through a powerful and unmistakable vocal style. \nHer performances are defined by expressive guitar work and dynamic solos\, incorporating whammy and wah effects that add a distinctive edge to her sound. Backed by longtime collaborators Sandy Hunter on drums and Adam Bell on bass\, her live shows reflect strong musical chemistry built through years of performance. \nThe Toronto Blues Society (TBS) is a non-profit organization dedicated to promoting and preserving the legacy of blues music. As it celebrates over 40 years of supporting the genre\, it continues to honour its roots while fostering future generations of artists. \nThis program is in partnership with the Toronto Blues Society (TBS).
URL:https://torontounion.ca/event/monday-blues-angelica-jones/
LOCATION:Union\, 65 Front Street West\, Toronto\, ON\, Canada
